{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"dying-dietary-bass","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Problem\n\nThe working amd64 Jira Data Center harness only boots inside a CI runner (arm64 hosts stall\nunder emulation — `tests/external/live_jira_dc/README.md`). So every live DC reconcile\nobservation currently costs a full ~2h push→CI cycle, which makes root-causing live-only DC\ndefects (e.g. bug `reckless-diabolic-kob` — rich-text stored as `None` + perpetual re-emit)\nprohibitively slow.\n\n## Approach\n\nReuse the EXISTING agentic-in-CI pattern (`scripts/jira_dc_capability_map.py` +\n`.github/workflows/jira-dc-capability-map.yml`, ticket 259b): boot the ephemeral DC ONCE, then\nrun an Opus agent on rebar's own `rebar.llm` runtime that performs MANY live experiments in\nthat single boot. Where capability-map's agent drives raw REST to *map* the image, this one\ndrives rebar's OWN reconcile primitives to *root-cause* a defect.\n\nNew files (test + CI only — no `src/rebar` change):\n- `tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_dc_richtext_agentic_probe.py` — an opt-in pytest module\n  that reuses the proven `bound_dc_issue` fixture chain (so the agent starts from the exact\n  `(repo, local_id, key)` the failing rich-text tests use, cutover `dc` on) and boots the\n  agent with two tools: `run_python(code)` (a persistent in-process REPL warm-started with the\n  transport, `compute_update_fields`, `WikiTextCodec`, `cutover_clients`, `dc.run_bridge`,\n  `rebar`) and `jira_rest(method, path, body)` (raw REST ground-truth). Returns a structured\n  `RichTextRca` finding, each experiment cited to evidence ids.\n- `.github/workflows/jira-dc-richtext-probe.yml` — a `workflow_dispatch`-only driver, same\n  guardrails as capability-map (throwaway ephemeral instance, `REBAR_MCP_READONLY=1`, agent\n  instructed to REPORT not fix), installing `[dev]` (LLM runtime) + `[jira-datacenter]`\n  (transport), uploading the finding + evidence artifact.\n\n## Portability\n\nThe investigator is a **pytest module gated by env** (`REBAR_DC_RICHTEXT_PROBE=1` +\n`REBAR_RUN_EXTERNAL=1` + an LLM credential + the harness skip markers), so it runs against ANY\nreachable live DC — a local `make jira-dc-up` instance or CI — not a single CI provider. The\nGitHub Actions workflow is one convenient trigger, not the only path; a contributor with a\nlocal DC + key runs the same test directly with `pytest`. It is inert on every ordinary run\n(opt-in off → skips), never on push/PR/schedule.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `test_dc_richtext_agentic_probe.py` exists, lint/format clean, and collects + skips\n      cleanly when the opt-in env is unset (no live DC required for collection).\n- [ ] The module reuses the existing `bound_dc_issue` / `dc_store_copy_repo` / `dc_transport`\n      fixtures rather than re-porting the bound-store bootstrap.\n- [ ] The agent is given `run_python` (persistent namespace) + `jira_rest` tools and returns a\n      registered structured `RichTextRca` contract; it asserts only that a finding was\n      produced (an investigation, not a correctness assertion — it must not fail merely\n      because the bug still reproduces).\n- [ ] `jira-dc-richtext-probe.yml` is `workflow_dispatch`-only (no push/PR/schedule), boots\n      the pinned DC image, installs both `[dev]` and `[jira-datacenter]`, requires an\n      `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` (loud fail if absent), sets `REBAR_MCP_READONLY=1`, and uploads the\n      finding + evidence artifact.\n- [ ] A `workflow_dispatch` run of the probe on `main` completes and uploads a `RichTextRca`\n      finding with cited experiment evidence.","id":"bc5d-ffba-006b-4241","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Reusable agentic in-CI Jira DC investigator (rich-text root-cause probe)"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787866613851413001,"uuid":"f9fa13e1-824f-4cf8-a001-6452aa4060e3"}